terminal share

Goal
- Share tmux-backed terminal sessions from main computer to other devices.
- Sessions survive client disconnects.
- New connection can take over session. Old connection gets disconnected.

Current layout
- 01_SERVER: Go host service with Uber Fx.
- 02_CLI: Go terminal client with Uber Fx.
- 03_ANDROID: reserved.
- 04_IOS: reserved.

Host
- Binary: `host`
- Requires `tmux` installed on host machine.
- API:
  - `GET /healthz`
  - `GET /api/sessions`
  - `POST /api/sessions`
  - `DELETE /api/sessions/{name}`
  - `GET /api/sessions/{name}/attach` websocket
- Env:
  - `AUTHORIZATION_TOKEN`
  - `HOST_ADDRESS`
  - `HOST_AUTH_TOKEN`
  - `HOST_DEFAULT_SHELL_PATH`
  - `HOST_TMUX_BINARY_PATH`
- If `AUTHORIZATION_TOKEN` is empty, host generates temporary token and prints it on startup.

Terminal
- Binary: `terminal`
- Auto-discovers hosts on local network with mDNS.
- Also includes saved hosts and default `http://127.0.0.1:8080`.
- Env:
  - `AUTHORIZATION_TOKEN`
  - `TERMINAL_SERVER_URL`
  - `TERMINAL_AUTH_TOKEN`

Setup
- `./setup.sh`
- Installs Homebrew, tmux, mise, project tools, lefthook, tests, builds.
- Updates `~/.tmux.conf` with extended-keys settings for tmux.
- Restarts tmux server so new settings apply immediately.

Run tests
- `make test`

Build
- `cd 01_SERVER && go build ./cmd/host`
- `cd 02_CLI && go build ./cmd/terminal`
